sweet-publish-iortc (boot-speed, docs/research/47-iortc-wait.md option a0): publish the IORTC resource from the platform expert so
IOKitInitializeTime's waitForService(resourceMatching("IORTC"), 30 s) returns at once instead of timing out (30.003 s gap in run bs-q2,
research 45 s2). There is NO real RTC: nothing reads one, getGMTTimeOfDay stays the IOPlatformExpert default (returns 0), so the
calendar is still 1970 + uptime, exactly as after the timeout today (osfmk/kern/clock.c clock_initialize_calendar, research 47 s1).
Boot-arg sweetiortc=0 skips the publish (the 30 s wait comes back) for an A/B run. Default (no boot-arg) = publish.
Facts, read from source (xnu-8796.141.3): the only waiter is IOKitInitializeTime (iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp:73-91, called from
bsd_init bsd/kern/bsd_init.c:688; the return value is ignored). PE_init_iokit -> StartIOKitMatching (osfmk/kern/startup.c:689,
pexpert/arm/pe_init.c:382) registers the root nub, i.e. platform matching starts about 100 lines of kernel_bootstrap_thread BEFORE
bsd_init (startup.c:790). waitForMatchingServiceWithToken first looks for an existing matched service, otherwise sets a matched
notification and sleeps with the timeout (iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp:6444-6552); so the wait ends whether publishResource runs
before the wait (found) or during it (notification wakes it). Matching is asynchronous (matching thread), so which one happens is
decided by the run log (SWEET: platform expert registered vs "using N buffer headers").
publishResource sets the property on IOResources and registerService()s it (iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp:4903-4917, research 47).
Not verified on hardware.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,20 @@
 	}
 	sweet_restart_start();
 	registerService();
+	{
+		/*
+		 * IORTC (patch 0123, research 47): no RTC exists on this port. Publishing the resource only ends the
+		 * 30 s waitForService in IOKitInitializeTime; the calendar stays 1970 + uptime. sweetiortc=0 keeps the wait.
+		 */
+		uint32_t iortc = 1;
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetiortc", &iortc, sizeof(iortc));
+		if (iortc != 0) {
+			publishResource("IORTC");
+			IOLog("SWEET RTC: published IORTC resource, no time source (calendar 1970 + uptime)\n");
+		} else {
+			IOLog("SWEET RTC: sweetiortc=0, IORTC not published (30 s wait stays)\n");
+		}
+	}
 	IOLog("SWEET: platform expert registered\n");
 	return true;
 }
